{
  "about": "Marathi glossary for drharshmaheshwari.com. Every Marathi translation must use these terms: tests/i18n.test.mjs checks that when an English text contains a term, its Marathi has one of the accepted forms (a substring match, so stems such as लठ्ठपण and पुराव cover the inflected forms; nukta and chandrabindu are ignored when comparing). Change a term here, then retranslate what uses it. docs/translation.md has the rules.",
  "register": "Everyday spoken Marathi that a family in Pune or Nagpur would use, not textbook Sanskritised Marathi, and Marathi grammar and words (आहे, नाही, साठी, वजन), never Hindi. Common English health words that people say in Marathi stay as they are said (BMI, ब्लड शुगर, डायबिटीस, ब्लड प्रेशर). Polite plural for the reader (तुम्ही) and for doctors (डॉक्टरांना). Short sentences. Numbers in 0-9, never Devanagari digits. Units as in English (cm, kg). Full stop is '.'.",
